.TH THERMOSERVICE 8 "2026-05-09" "thermoservice 0.7" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
thermoservice \- Flask web service exposing DS18B20 temperature readings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gunicorn
.RI \-b " 0.0.0.0:5000" " \-w " "4 thermoservice:app"
.br
(managed automatically via systemd)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B thermoservice
is a lightweight Flask application that reads temperature data from a DS18B20
1-Wire sensor and exposes it over HTTP.  Under normal operation it is started
automatically by systemd and served by
.BR gunicorn (1)
on port
.BR 5000 .
.PP
When the 1-Wire kernel module is enabled (
.BR w1-therm ), the service reads
.I /sys/bus/w1/devices/28*/w1_slave
and makes the current temperature available via a JSON endpoint and a
browser-friendly HTML page.
.SH HTTP ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B GET /
HTML dashboard showing the hostname, current timestamp, and temperature.
.TP
.B GET /celsius
JSON response with the following fields:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
.B temperature
\(em temperature in degrees Celsius (float, or null if no sensor)
.IP \(bu 4
.B rom
\(em sensor ROM identifier string
.IP \(bu 4
.B sensor
\(em hostname of the device
.IP \(bu 4
.B time
\(em timestamp of the reading
.IP \(bu 4
.B error
\(em present only when no sensor is detected
.RE
.TP
.B GET /logo.svg
The service SVG icon.
.TP
.B GET /favicon.ico
Browser favicon.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/thermoservice/thermoservice.py
Flask application entry point.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/thermoservice.service
systemd service unit.
.TP
.I /sys/bus/w1/devices/28*/w1_slave
Kernel 1-Wire sysfs interface for DS18B20 sensors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FLASK_CONFIG
Set to
.I production
by the systemd unit.
.TP
.B FLASK_APP
Set to
.I thermoservice.py
by the systemd unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thermo (1),
.BR ha_push (8),
.BR gunicorn (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
